  "aiContextParagraph": "The political landscape in Kenya is marked by growing friction between President William Ruto and his former deputy, Rigathi Gachagua. Recent developments show Gachagua asserting influence within the Mt Kenya region, setting a December deadline for local leaders to pivot their political alignment away from the current administration. Gachagua has further focused on the internal processes of the Democratic Congress Party, suggesting that party nominations by March 2027 should be viewed as a definitive step for candidates seeking office. Meanwhile, President Ruto has maintained a critical stance toward his opponents, engaging in public discourse regarding electoral conduct and regional political allegiances. Observers note that these exchanges highlight shifting alliances and internal competition within the ruling coalition as political figures prepare for the upcoming electoral cycle and party-level selection processes.",
